---
// Italian variant of WhatSpecScoreIs.astro.
// HTML structure + CSS classes match the English original exactly so the
// shared global rules and the page-level layout behave identically.
// Tab labels translate (idea / feature / plan stay because they ARE the
// SpecScore artifact type names); the artifact example content stays English
// because that IS the SpecScore format (Markdown + English keywords like
// Status, Promotes To, AC-1, GIVEN/WHEN/THEN).
//
// JS for the tab strip queries `.wi-tab` and `.wi-track` — same class
// names as the English component.
---

<section class="what-is section" aria-labelledby="what-is-title">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <h2 id="what-is-title" class="what-is__title">
      Un formato per le specifiche che già scrivi.
    </h2>
    <div class="what-is__grid">
      <div class="what-is__col what-is__col--text">
        <p class="what-is__intro">
          <strong>SpecScore è un formato Markdown + YAML</strong> per feature,
          requisiti e criteri di accettazione. Definisce una struttura che il tuo
          team e i tuoi agenti IA capiscono entrambi — ed è semplicemente composto
          da file nel tuo repository.
        </p>
        <p class="what-is__intro">
          Un progetto SpecScore è formato da tre tipi di artefatti lungo un
          ciclo di vita: un'<strong>Idea</strong> cattura una direzione
          abbozzata; una specifica di <strong>Feature</strong> congela il
          comportamento concordato; un <strong>Plan</strong> scompone la
          feature in task ordinati, ciascuno dei quali cita i criteri di
          accettazione che soddisfa.
        </p>

        <p class="what-is__intro">
          <strong>Perché è importante per il tuo agente.</strong> Poiché la
          struttura è leggibile dalla macchina, gli agenti IA possono
          interrogare la specifica tramite la CLI invece di leggere ogni
          singolo file. Chiedi <em>«su cosa dovrei lavorare adesso?»</em> e
          la CLI restituisce le Feature aperte e le domande irrisolte.
          La stessa forma che il tuo team revisiona; molto meno contesto che
          l'agente deve caricare.
        </p>

        <figure
          class="what-is__diagram"
          aria-label="Gerarchia SpecScore. Una Feature contiene Requisiti (R1, R2, R3). Ciascun Requisito contiene Criteri di accettazione (AC). Gli scenari sono sotto."
        >
          <svg
            viewBox="0 0 760 320"
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            role="img"
            aria-hidden="true"
            class="what-is__diagram-svg"
          >
            <text x="20" y="36" class="wf-annot">FIG. 1</text>

            <rect x="310" y="20" width="140" height="44" rx="2" class="wf-node" />
            <text x="380" y="48" text-anchor="middle" class="wf-label">FEATURE</text>

            <path d="M 380 64 V 88 H 140 V 110" class="wf-line" />
            <path d="M 380 64 V 88 H 380 V 110" class="wf-line" />
            <path d="M 380 64 V 88 H 620 V 110" class="wf-line" />

            <rect x="80"  y="110" width="120" height="40" rx="2" class="wf-node" />
            <text x="140" y="135" text-anchor="middle" class="wf-label">R1</text>

            <rect x="320" y="110" width="120" height="40" rx="2" class="wf-node" />
            <text x="380" y="135" text-anchor="middle" class="wf-label">R2</text>

            <rect x="560" y="110" width="120" height="40" rx="2" class="wf-node" />
            <text x="620" y="135" text-anchor="middle" class="wf-label">R3</text>

            <path d="M 140 150 V 178" class="wf-line" />
            <path d="M 380 150 V 178" class="wf-line" />
            <path d="M 620 150 V 178" class="wf-line" />

            <text x="140" y="198" text-anchor="middle" class="wf-label-small">AC-1, AC-2</text>
            <text x="380" y="198" text-anchor="middle" class="wf-label-small">AC-1, AC-2</text>
            <text x="620" y="198" text-anchor="middle" class="wf-label-small">AC-1 … AC-3</text>

            <path d="M 140 214 V 240 H 380 V 240" class="wf-line" />
            <path d="M 380 214 V 240" class="wf-line" />
            <path d="M 620 214 V 240 H 380" class="wf-line" />
            <path d="M 380 240 V 256" class="wf-line" />

            <rect x="290" y="256" width="180" height="44" rx="2" class="wf-node" />
            <text x="380" y="284" text-anchor="middle" class="wf-label">GIVEN / WHEN / THEN</text>
          </svg>
          <figcaption class="what-is__diagram-cap">
            Feature → Requirements → Acceptance Criteria → Scenarios.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <div class="what-is__col what-is__col--example">
        <div class="wi-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Ciclo di vita degli artefatti SpecScore">
          <button type="button" role="tab" id="wi-tab-idea"    aria-controls="wi-panel-idea"    aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="wi-tab"           data-step="0">idea</button>
          <span class="wi-tab-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <button type="button" role="tab" id="wi-tab-feature" aria-controls="wi-panel-feature" aria-selected="true"  tabindex="0"  class="wi-tab is-active" data-step="1">feature</button>
          <span class="wi-tab-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <button type="button" role="tab" id="wi-tab-plan"    aria-controls="wi-panel-plan"    aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" class="wi-tab"           data-step="2">plan</button>
        </div>

        <div class="wi-viewport">
          <div class="wi-track" data-index="1" style="transform: translateX(-33.3333%);">

            <div class="wi-panel" role="tabpanel" id="wi-panel-idea" aria-labelledby="wi-tab-idea">
              <div class="what-is__example">
                <div class="what-is__example-head">
                  <span class="what-is__example-label">ESEMPIO</span>
                  <span class="what-is__example-path">ideas/apply-discount.md</span>
                </div>
<pre class="what-is__example-code"><code><span class="sx-h1"># Idea: Discount codes at checkout</span>

<span class="sx-bold">**Status:**</span> approved
<span class="sx-bold">**Promotes To:**</span> features/checkout/apply-discount.md
<span class="sx-bold">**Author:**</span> cart-team

<span class="sx-h2">## Why</span>

Checkout drop-off is high at the payment step; users
leave to search for coupons and never return. Let them
paste codes directly in the cart before starting checkout.

<span class="sx-h2">## Success Criteria</span>

- Users enter promo codes without leaving the cart
- Invalid codes fail fast with actionable copy
- Stacking rules are clear (only one code per order)

<span class="sx-h2">## Outstanding Questions</span>

- What happens if a cart's subtotal drops below the
  code's minimum spend after applying?
- Do we support percentage and flat discounts in v1?</code></pre>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="wi-panel" role="tabpanel" id="wi-panel-feature" aria-labelledby="wi-tab-feature">
              <div class="what-is__example">
                <div class="what-is__example-head">
                  <span class="what-is__example-label">ESEMPIO</span>
                  <span class="what-is__example-path">features/checkout/apply-discount.md</span>
                </div>
<pre class="what-is__example-code"><code><span class="sx-fm">---
title: Apply Discount Code at Checkout
status: approved
created: 2026-04-12
promoted_from: ideas/apply-discount.md
---</span>

<span class="sx-h2"># Context</span>

Shoppers with a valid coupon code want to apply it
before payment so they can see the reduced total.

<span class="sx-h2"># Requirements</span>

<span class="sx-h3">## R1 — Code validation</span>
Accept coupon codes up to 16 alphanumeric characters.

- <span class="sx-bold">AC-1:</span> Given a valid code, when applied,
  then subtotal decreases by the code's value.
- <span class="sx-bold">AC-2:</span> Given an expired code, when applied,
  then show error "This code has expired".
- <span class="sx-bold">AC-3:</span> Given an empty input, the apply button
  remains disabled.

<span class="sx-h3">## R2 — Single-use enforcement</span>
Enforce one promo code per cart. Applying a second
code replaces the first after confirmation.

- <span class="sx-bold">AC-1:</span> Given a cart with an active code, when a
  second code is applied, then prompt to replace.

<span class="sx-h2"># Outstanding Questions</span>

None at this time.</code></pre>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="wi-panel" role="tabpanel" id="wi-panel-plan" aria-labelledby="wi-tab-plan">
              <div class="what-is__example">
                <div class="what-is__example-head">
                  <span class="what-is__example-label">ESEMPIO</span>
                  <span class="what-is__example-path">plans/apply-discount/README.md</span>
                </div>
<pre class="what-is__example-code"><code><span class="sx-h1"># Plan: Apply Discount</span>

<span class="sx-bold">**Status:**</span> approved
<span class="sx-bold">**Features:**</span>
  - <span class="sx-tick">[apply-discount](../../features/apply-discount.md)</span>
<span class="sx-bold">**Author:**</span> cart-team
<span class="sx-bold">**Effort:**</span> M
<span class="sx-bold">**Impact:**</span> high

<span class="sx-h2">## Context</span>

The <span class="sx-tick">apply-discount</span> Feature is Approved. This plan
breaks it into ordered tasks; each task cites the
acceptance criteria it satisfies.

<span class="sx-h2">## Tasks</span>

<span class="sx-h3">### T1 — Accept a `code` field on the cart</span>
Cites: R1.AC-1, R1.AC-2, R1.AC-3

<span class="sx-h3">### T2 — Validate code time-window</span>
Cites: R2.AC-1, R2.AC-2

<span class="sx-h3">### T3 — Apply percentage to subtotal, round down</span>
Cites: R3.AC-1, R3.AC-2

<span class="sx-h3">### T4 — Higher-of tiebreak vs site-wide promo</span>
Cites: R3.AC-3

<span class="sx-h3">### T5 — Confirmation toast on apply / replace</span>
Cites: R1.AC-2</code></pre>
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>
